From what I remember, there was some sort of wager between the
dwarven lord and Loki as to who is better craftsman. Each other's 
head was at stake... 
Mjollnir is one of them, a present by the dwarven lord to Odin's 
son, Thor. Apparently, while the DL was making this hammer, Loki tried 
to disturb him by assuming the form of a bee, as a result of which the 
hammer has a defect: the handle is shorter than ideal. 
DL won the bet, however.

The epilogue is that Gods decided that DL won because of Mjollnir.
However, Loki saved his head claiming that though he lost his head,
nobody could touch his neck or something (a la Portia) 

This is to the best of my recollection, there may be lots of errors
in it though.

